# Test Conventions (Python)

Apply when editing `tests/**/*.py`. Read [doc/stack.md](../../doc/stack.md). Subagent: `test-agent`.

## What tests document

Test code explains **What** — behavior under test, not implementation steps.

## Naming

Full rules: [doc/coding-conventions.md](../../doc/coding-conventions.md), patterns: [test-code-patterns.md](../../.cursor/skills/spec-test-design/references/test-code-patterns.md).

| Target | Convention | Example |
|--------|------------|---------|
| Test files | `test_<feature>.py` | `test_user_service.py` |
| Test functions | `test_tc_NNN_<what>` | `test_tc_001_returns_404_when_item_missing` |

- Include TC ID from `doc/testspec-*.md`
- Use `@pytest.mark.parametrize` `id=` with TC ID for table-driven cases

## Layout

- `tests/unit/`, `tests/integration/` when project uses them
- Mirror `src/` structure when practical

## Determinism

- Mock network, DB, time, filesystem
- Use `tmp_path` / fixtures for I/O
- No live external services in unit tests

## Testspec alignment

- TC IDs match `doc/testspec-*.md`

## Commands

Use `test_single` / `test_all` from `doc/stack.md` (e.g. `uv run pytest`).
